        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Keir Starmer's Labour braces for heavy losses in UK local elections Europe Issued on: 08/05/2026 - 11:43 The far right are making gains in England as the results of local elections are counted overnight. The governing Labour party has lost control of a number of councils... and pressure is piling on Prime Minister Keir Starmer. While most results won’t be declared until later Friday, Reform UK — led by populist Nigel Farage — is on course for a major victory. Details by FRANCE 24’s correspondent in London, Bénédicte Paviot. Russia and Ukraine trade major attacks despite Victory Day ceasefire 08/05/2026 Europe Putin's 'paranoia': 'He's fearful of Ukrainians & afraid the elite around him is starting to break' 08/05/2026 Europe 'Ici c'est Paris': Defending champions PSG 'on the verge of making history' 07/05/2026 Sport 3 patients are being evacuated to Europe from ship with hantavirus outbreak 06/05/2026 Europe War in Ukraine: Russia attacks east and south Ukraine with over 100 drones 06/05/2026 Europe Hantavirus-hit cruise ship heads to Spain to dock in Canary Islands 06/05/2026 Europe Kyiv says Russia broke unilateral ceasefire with drone and missile attacks 06/05/2026 Europe Russia launches deadly attack in Ukraine: At least 28 killed 06/05/2026 Europe Venice Biennale faces outcry over Israel and Russia's participation 06/05/2026 Europe"
